      "text": "Given that the fifth term of the arithmetic sequence is \\(11\\) and the common difference \\(d\\) is \\(1\\), we first need to determine the first term \\(a_1\\) of the sequence.\n\nThe \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by the formula:\n\\[\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n\\]\nFor the fifth term (\\(n=5\\)):\n\\[\na_5 = a_1 + (5-1)d = a_1 + 4d\n\\]\nWe know that \\(a_5 = 11\\) and \\(d = 1\\), so:\n\\[\n11 = a_1 + 4 \\cdot 1\n\\]\n\\[\n11 = a_1 + 4\n\\]\nSolving for \\(a_1\\):\n\\[\na_1 = 11 - 4 = 7\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the first two terms of the sequence. The first term \\(a_1\\) is \\(7\\) and the second term \\(a_2\\) is:\n\\[\na_2 = a_1 + d = 7 + 1 = 8\n\\]\n\nThe product of the first two terms is:\n\\[\na_1 \\cdot a_2 = 7 \\cdot 8 = 56\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of the first two terms is \\(\\boxed{56}\\).",
